  "name": "l2-padding-v1",
  "description": "L2-1 (crypto ABI 23) size buckets for key packages and Welcomes: 256-byte steps (at least one block) up to 4096 bytes, then the next power of two up to 8 MiB; above 8 MiB nothing is padded (padded: null). The pad is one MLS extension of type 0xF0A2 whose data is zero bytes, inside the signed key package and inside the encrypted GroupInfo. key_package_hex is a padded key package from the Rust core (identity acct_vector/dev_vector) for the server's structural check; regenerate with the ignored Rust test l2::tests::print_vector_key_package.",
